{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "18", "x": 0.9076798674721437, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.026063381131492046, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "F", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.01859382309708816, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Any prospect of the elm returning relies heavily on trees being either", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.7654918280947696, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "resistant to, or tolerant of, the disease. This means a widespread reintroduction", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.8263778097860683, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "would involve existing or new hybrid strains derived from resistant, generally non-", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.82133112145998, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "native elm species. A new generation of seedlings have been bred and tested to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.8259686326954333, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "see if they can withstand the fungus by cutting a small slit on the bark and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.8264695696197236, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "injecting a tiny amount of the pathogen. 'The effects are very quick,' says Russell.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.8261641477823392, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "'You return in four to six weeks and trees that are resistant show no symptoms,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2930660423122369, "w": 0.8260552662813984, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "whereas those that are susceptible show leaf loss and may even have died", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.32139637352567824, "w": 0.8267764268064615, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "completely.'", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3497267990426009, "w": 0.12985500510933107, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "G", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.38799500085929334, "w": 0.021818989015784024, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "All of this raises questions of social acceptance, acknowledges Russell. 'If", "x": 0.16774843308549978, "y": 0.38799500085929334, "w": 0.765643975126216, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "we're putting elm back into the landscape, a small element of it is not native - are", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.41632538865482344, "w": 0.8267860641521192, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "we bothered about that?' For her, the environmental case for reintroducing elm is", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4446557764503536, "w": 0.8267037366142139, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "strong. 'They will host wildlife, which is a good thing.' Others are more wary. 'On", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.47301087175797835, "w": 0.8267133739598715, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "the face of it, it seems like a good idea,' says Elliot. The problem, he suggests, is", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5013412218321159, "w": 0.8258808713349765, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "that, 'You're replacing a native species with a horticultural analogue*. You're", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5295232891122934, "w": 0.8267272148286352, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "effectively cloning.' There's also the risk of introducing new diseases. Rather than", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.557853639186431, "w": 0.8264254838895876, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "plant new elms, the Woodland Trust emphasises providing space to those elms", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5861840269819611, "w": 0.8265171411982891, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "that have survived independently. 'Sometimes the best thing you can do is just", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6145143770560988, "w": 0.8258922516048487, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "give nature time to recover ... over time, you might get resistance,' says Elliot.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6428448025730215, "w": 0.7865102638243878, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "* horticultural analogue: a cultivated plant species that is genetically similar to an", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6811501222399445, "w": 0.8267723258083093, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "existing species", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7094804723140822, "w": 0.1689600217270882, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}